      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Structure of Indian Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the supreme monetary authority and regulatory body of the Indian Banking System.",
        "Key functions of the RBI encompass monetary policy formulation, currency issuance, and regulation of commercial banks.",
        "Bank Nationalisation in India took place primarily in two phases: 14 major banks in 1969 and 6 additional banks in 1980.",
        "Understanding various types of bank accounts (Savings, Current, FD, RD) and core banking terminology is crucial for banking exam preparation."
      ],
      "id": "flof3u5"
    },
